/-!
# Isolated singularities: the completion of a deformation is the family of completed henselizations

**Stacks 0DZF** proves that the chain
`𝓓_P → ∏ 𝓓_{P_{𝔪 i}} → ∏ 𝓓_{P^h_{𝔪 i}} → ∏ 𝓓_{P^∧_{𝔪 i}}`
has smooth maps inducing isomorphisms on tangent spaces, and it does so without treating the
three maps one at a time: it applies **Stacks 0DZ5** to `P` *itself* with
`J = 𝔪 1 ∩ … ∩ 𝔪 n` — where the finite type hypothesis of 0DZ5 genuinely holds, which it does
not at any of the local rings — and then says "`P^∧ = ∏ P^∧_{𝔪 i}`".

This file makes that step precise, with the last term read as the completion of the
henselization. The comparison it proves is an isomorphism of functors over `𝒞_Λ`: completing a
deformation of `P` along `J` and then transporting along a ring isomorphism
`P^∧_J ≅ ∏ (P^h_{𝔪 i})^∧` gives the *same* functor as localizing at each `𝔪 i`, henselizing,
completing each henselized local ring, and reading the resulting family as a deformation of the
product ring. Both the ring isomorphism and its description on elements coming from `P` are
inputs, so that a caller may supply the one it already has; the composite isomorphism built from
`Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv` and
`Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionHenselizedLocalRingEquiv` is supplied here too.

The comparison is what lets the conclusions of Stacks 0DZ5 at `(P, J)`, which hold for the
composite functor, be read off for the chain as it is actually built — through
`Deformation.isSmooth_of_iso` and `Deformation.mapIsomorphismClasses_eq_of_iso`, both of which
consume an isomorphism of *based* functors; so the comparison is packaged as one, through the
recognition principle `Deformation.Examples.basedIsoOfFiberEquiv`, which is
`CategoryTheory.BasedNatIso.mkNatIso` fed with a family of ring isomorphisms of the fibres.

## Main definitions

* `Deformation.Examples.completionUnit`: the canonical map from the fibre of a deformation to the
  fibre of its completion.
* `Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv`: the composite ring isomorphism
  `P^∧_J ≅ ∏ (P_{𝔪 i})^∧ ≅ ∏ (P^h_{𝔪 i})^∧`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.henselizationDeformation_ideal_comap`: the inverse image in a henselized
  deformation of the ideal `J P^h` is generated by the inverse image of `J`.
* `Deformation.Examples.deformation_ideal_comap_fg`: the inverse image of a finitely generated
  ideal under the reduction map of a deformation is finitely generated.
* `Deformation.Examples.apply_algebraMap_eq_zero_of_mem_maximalIdeal`: the reduction map of a
  deformation kills the maximal ideal of its Artinian base.
* `Deformation.Examples.completionUnit_algebraMap`: the canonical map into the fibre of a
  completed deformation is linear over the Artinian base.
* `Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_henselizedFiber`,
  `Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizedFiber` and
  `Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizationFamilyFiber`: the
  fibre of the completed deformation is the completion of the fibre; at one point, and for the
  whole family, it is the family of completions of the henselized localized fibres.
* `Deformation.Examples.apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv`: the decomposition
  `R^∧_J ≅ ∏ (R_{𝔪 i})^∧` on elements coming from `R`.
* `Deformation.Examples.piDeformation_algebraMap_base` and
  `Deformation.Examples.piDeformationFunctor_map_apply`: a product of deformations is componentwise
  on the structural map from the base and on morphisms.
* `Deformation.Examples.algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv` and
  `Deformation.Examples.apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv`: the composite ring
  isomorphism is `k`-linear and is described on elements coming from `P`.
* `Deformation.Examples.nonempty_basedIso_adicCompletionFunctor_completionFunctors`: **the
  comparison**, as an isomorphism of based functors over `𝒞_Λ`.

## Implementation notes

The three functors of the chain are recorded in the repository as *data* — a
`Deformation.Examples.LocalizationFunctorData`, a
`Deformation.Examples.HenselizationFunctorData` and a
`Deformation.Examples.AdicCompletionFunctorData` — chosen by `Classical.choice`, so the
identification of the Artinian base of a value of one of them with the base of its argument is
not definitional: it is the equality `CategoryTheory.BasedFunctor.w_obj` of objects of `𝒞_Λ`, and
every clause about the structural map from the base has to be read through it. That is what the
`eqToHom` in the statements below is doing, and the one-line helpers at the top of the file,
together with those of
`StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.IsolatedSingularitiesHenselizationComparison`, are the
arithmetic of those identifications.

The fibre of a *localized* deformation is likewise only *a* localization of the fibre at the
inverse image of the prime, not the chosen `Localization`; the two are identified by
`IsLocalization.algEquiv`, which is where
`Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizedFiber` starts.

The comparison takes the completion functor at `(P, J)` to be the canonical
`Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionFunctor`, rather than an arbitrary datum, because the target
of the comparison is `Deformation.Examples.completionFunctors`, which is built from the canonical
one. The intermediate results are stated for an arbitrary datum, since nothing in them needs the
choice.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DZF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DZF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DZ5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DZ5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DYV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DYV)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe uι u w

namespace Deformation.Examples

attribute [local instance 100] henselizationAlgebra

variable {Λ : Type u} {k : Type w} [CommRing Λ] [Field k] [Algebra Λ k]
  {P : Type w} [CommRing P] [Algebra k P]

/-! ### The arithmetic of the identifications of Artinian bases -/

/-- Transport of membership in the maximal ideal along an equality of objects of `𝒞_Λ`. -/
private theorem mem_maximalIdeal_eqToHom_hom
    {A B : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, w, w} Λ k} (h : A = B) {a : (A : Type w)}
    (ha : a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (A : Type w)) :
    (eqToHom h).hom a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B : Type w) := by
  subst h
  exact ha

/-- Transport along five equalities of objects of `𝒞_Λ` is transport along any proof of the
composite equality. -/
private theorem eqToHom_hom_trans₅ {A₀ A₁ A₂ A₃ A₄ A₅ : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, w, w} Λ k}
    (h₁ : A₀ = A₁) (h₂ : A₁ = A₂) (h₃ : A₂ = A₃) (h₄ : A₃ = A₄) (h₅ : A₄ = A₅)
    (h : A₀ = A₅) (a : (A₀ : Type w)) :
    (eqToHom h₅).hom ((eqToHom h₄).hom ((eqToHom h₃).hom
        ((eqToHom h₂).hom ((eqToHom h₁).hom a)))) = (eqToHom h).hom a := by
  subst h₁ h₂ h₃ h₄ h₅
  rfl

/-- Evaluation of a dependent product of rings at an index, on elements. -/
private theorem evalRingHom_apply {ιv : Type uι} (R : ιv → Type w) [∀ i, CommRing (R i)]
    (i : ιv) (x : ∀ i, R i) : Pi.evalRingHom R i x = x i := rfl

/-- Transport of a family of ring isomorphisms to the products, on components. -/
private theorem piCongrRight_apply {ιv : Type uι} {R S : ιv → Type w}
    [∀ i, CommRing (R i)] [∀ i, CommRing (S i)] (f : ∀ i, R i ≃+* S i) (x : ∀ i, R i) (i : ιv) :
    RingEquiv.piCongrRight f x i = f i (x i) := rfl

/-- The canonical map on completions, evaluated on the image of an element. -/
private theorem adicCompletionMap_apply_algebraMap {R S : Type w} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) (I : Ideal R) (J : Ideal S) (h : I.map f ≤ J) (r : R) :
    adicCompletionMap f I J h (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion I R) r) =
      algebraMap S (AdicCompletion J S) (f r) := by
  simpa using RingHom.congr_fun (adicCompletionMap_comp_algebraMap f I J h) r

/-! ### Generic ring-theoretic input -/

/-- **The inverse image of an extended ideal under a surjection out of a flat algebra.** Let
`π : Q → S` and `ρ : F → H` be surjective, let `a : Q → F` and `g : S → H` make the square
commute, and let the kernel of `ρ` be contained in the image ideal `a(π⁻¹(J)) F`. Then the
inverse image under `ρ` of the extended ideal `J H` is exactly `a(π⁻¹(J)) F`. -/
private theorem comap_map_eq_map_comap
    {Q F H S : Type w} [CommRing Q] [CommRing F] [CommRing H] [CommRing S]
    (π : Q →+* S) (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (a : Q →+* F)
    (ρ : F →+* H) (hρ : Function.Surjective ρ) (g : S →+* H)
    (hcomm : ∀ x, ρ (a x) = g (π x)) (J : Ideal S)
    (hk : RingHom.ker ρ ≤ (J.comap π).map a) :
    (J.map g).comap ρ = (J.comap π).map a := by
  have hge : J.map g ≤ ((J.comap π).map a).map ρ := by
    refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun s hs => Ideal.mem_comap.mpr ?_
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hπ s
    rw [← hx, ← hcomm x]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem ρ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem a (Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (hx ▸ hs)))
  refine le_antisymm (fun y hy => ?_) (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨z, hz, hbz⟩ := (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective ρ hρ).mp
      (hge (Ideal.mem_comap.mp hy))
    have hyz : y - z ∈ RingHom.ker ρ := by
      rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, hbz, sub_self]
    simpa using Ideal.add_mem ((J.comap π).map a) (hk hyz) hz
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_comap, hcomm x]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem g (Ideal.mem_comap.mp hx)

/-- **An ideal contained in an extended maximal ideal is contained in the inverse image of `J`.**
The map `g` out of the Artinian base factors as `a ∘ f`, and `f` carries the maximal ideal into
`π⁻¹(J)`; this is the shape in which the kernel bound of a deformation is used. -/
private theorem le_map_comap_of_le_map
    {B Q F S : Type w} [CommRing B] [CommRing Q] [CommRing F] [CommRing S]
    (π : Q →+* S) (a : Q →+* F) (J : Ideal S) (m : Ideal B) (g : B →+* F) (f : B → Q)
    (K : Ideal F) (hK : K ≤ m.map g)
    (hg : ∀ b, g b = a (f b)) (hf : ∀ b ∈ m, π (f b) ∈ J) :
    K ≤ (J.comap π).map a := by
  refine hK.trans (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun b hb => ?_)
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, hg b]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem a (Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (hf b hb))

/-- **Finite generation of the inverse image of a finitely generated ideal under a surjection
whose kernel is an extended ideal.** -/
private theorem fg_comap_of_surjective_of_ker_eq
    {Q S B : Type w} [CommRing Q] [CommRing S] [CommRing B]
    (π : Q →+* S) (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (g : B →+* Q) (m : Ideal B) (hm : m.FG)
    (hker : RingHom.ker π = m.map g) (J : Ideal S) (hJ : J.FG) :
    (J.comap π).FG := by
  have hle : RingHom.ker π ≤ J.comap π := fun x hx => by simp [RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx]
  refine Ideal.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker_of_surjective (f := π) ?_ ?_ hπ
  · rwa [Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective π hπ J]
  · rw [inf_eq_right.mpr hle, hker]
    exact hm.map g

/-! ### The ideal of a henselized deformation -/

/-- **The reduction map of a deformation kills the maximal ideal of its Artinian base.** The
reduction of the structural map from the base is the structural map of `P` composed with the
augmentation, and the maximal ideal of the base is the kernel of the augmentation. -/
public theorem apply_algebraMap_eq_zero_of_mem_maximalIdeal
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P)
    {y : (X.left.base : Type w)}
    (hy : y ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.left.base : Type w)) :
    X.hom.map.hom (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber y) = 0 := by
  have hw := congrArg
    (fun f : CommRingCat.of (X.left.base : Type w) ⟶ CommRingCat.of P => f.hom y)
    X.hom.cartesian.w
  change X.hom.map.hom (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber y) =
    algebraMap k P (X.hom.base.hom.toRingHom y) at hw
  have hbase : RingHom.ker X.hom.base.hom.toRingHom =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.left.base : Type w) :=
    IsLocalRing.ker_eq_maximalIdeal (R := (X.left.base : Type w)) (K := k)
      X.hom.base.hom.toRingHom (deformationBaseMap_surjective X)
  have hz : X.hom.base.hom.toRingHom y = (0 : k) := RingHom.mem_ker.mp (hbase.symm ▸ hy)
  rw [hw, hz, map_zero]
  rfl

/-- **The inverse image of the henselized ideal in a henselized deformation.** For a deformation
`X` of `P` with reduction `π : Q → P`, the inverse image in the fibre of the henselized
deformation of the ideal `J P^h` is the ideal generated by the image of `π⁻¹(J)`.

Both inclusions come from `π` being surjective: the image of `π⁻¹(J) Q^h` in `P^h` is `J P^h`,
and the kernel of the reduction of the henselized deformation lies in `π⁻¹(J) Q^h`, because that
kernel is generated by the maximal ideal of the Artinian base and the reduction of a deformation
kills that ideal. -/
public theorem henselizationDeformation_ideal_comap (J : Ideal P)
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P) :
    (J.map (algebraMap P (henselization P J : Type w))).comap
        ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J).functor.obj X).hom.map.hom =
      (J.comap X.hom.map.hom).map
        ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J).henselizationMap X) := by
  set H := henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J with hHdef
  refine comap_map_eq_map_comap X.hom.map.hom (deformationSpecialFiberMap_surjective X)
    (H.henselizationMap X) (H.functor.obj X).hom.map.hom
    (deformationSpecialFiberMap_surjective (H.functor.obj X))
    (algebraMap P (henselization P J : Type w)) (H.specialFiber_comm X) J ?_
  refine le_map_comap_of_le_map X.hom.map.hom (H.henselizationMap X) J
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((H.functor.obj X).left.base : Type w))
    (algebraMap (((H.functor.obj X).left.base : Type w)) (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber)
    (fun b => algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber
      ((eqToHom (H.functor.w_obj X)).hom b))
    (RingHom.ker (H.functor.obj X).hom.map.hom)
    (deformationSpecialFiber_ker_le_map_maximalIdeal (H.functor.obj X))
    (fun b => (henselizationMap_algebraMap H X b).symm) (fun b hb => ?_)
  rw [apply_algebraMap_eq_zero_of_mem_maximalIdeal X
    (mem_maximalIdeal_eqToHom_hom (H.functor.w_obj X) hb)]
  exact J.zero_mem

/-- **The inverse image of a finitely generated ideal under the reduction map of a deformation is
finitely generated.** The reduction `π : Q → P` is surjective with kernel generated by the
maximal ideal of the Artinian base, so `π⁻¹(J)` has finitely generated image `J` and finitely
generated intersection with the kernel. -/
public theorem deformation_ideal_comap_fg (J : Ideal P) (hJ : J.FG)
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P) :
    (J.comap X.hom.map.hom).FG := by
  have hker : RingHom.ker X.hom.map.hom =
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.left.base : Type w)).map
        (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber) :=
    le_antisymm (deformationSpecialFiber_ker_le_map_maximalIdeal X)
      (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun y hy => Ideal.mem_comap.mpr
        (RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (apply_algebraMap_eq_zero_of_mem_maximalIdeal X hy)))
  exact fg_comap_of_surjective_of_ker_eq X.hom.map.hom
    (deformationSpecialFiberMap_surjective X)
    (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber)
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.left.base : Type w)) (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _)
    hker J hJ

/-! ### The canonical map into the fibre of a completed deformation -/

/-- The canonical map from the fibre of a deformation to the fibre of its completion: the
structural map into the adic completion of the fibre, read through the identification of that
completion with the fibre of the completed deformation. -/
public noncomputable def completionUnit
    {R : Type w} [CommRing R] [Algebra k R] (I : Ideal R)
    (C : AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k) R I)
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) R) :
    X.left.fiber →+* (C.functor.obj X).left.fiber :=
  (C.fiberEquiv X).symm.toRingHom.comp
    (algebraMap X.left.fiber (AdicCompletion (I.comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber))

/-- **The canonical map into the fibre of a completed deformation is a map of algebras over the
Artinian base.** This is the base-compatibility clause of the completion datum, read through the
identification of the base of the completed deformation with the base of the deformation. -/
public theorem completionUnit_algebraMap
    {R : Type w} [CommRing R] [Algebra k R] (I : Ideal R)
    (C : AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k) R I) (hC : C.IsBaseCompatible)
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) R)
    (a : ((C.functor.obj X).left.base : Type w)) :
    completionUnit I C X
        (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber
          ((eqToHom (C.functor.w_obj X)).hom a)) =
      algebraMap (((C.functor.obj X).left.base : Type w)) (C.functor.obj X).left.fiber a := by
  apply (C.fiberEquiv X).injective
  have hL : (C.fiberEquiv X) (completionUnit I C X
      (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber
        ((eqToHom (C.functor.w_obj X)).hom a))) =
      algebraMap X.left.fiber (AdicCompletion (I.comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber)
        (algebraMap ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber
          ((eqToHom (C.functor.w_obj X)).hom a)) :=
    (C.fiberEquiv X).apply_symm_apply _
  rw [hL, hC X a]
  exact (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply ((X.left.base : Type w)) X.left.fiber
    (AdicCompletion (I.comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber)
    ((eqToHom (C.functor.w_obj X)).hom a)).symm

/-! ### The fibre of the completion of a henselized deformation -/

/-- **The fibre of the completion of a henselized deformation is the completion of the fibre.**
Completing the fibre of a deformation `X` of `P` at `π⁻¹(J)`, and henselizing the fibre and then
completing at the inverse image of `J P^h`, give the same ring: the henselization map of the
pair `(Q, π⁻¹(J))` is an isomorphism on the completions, and by
`Deformation.Examples.henselizationDeformation_ideal_comap` the two ideals being completed at
correspond. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_henselizedFiber (J : Ideal P)
    (C : AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k) (henselization P J : Type w)
      (J.map (algebraMap P (henselization P J : Type w))))
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P) :
    ∃ e : AdicCompletion (J.comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber ≃+*
        (C.functor.obj
          ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J).functor.obj X)).left.fiber,
      ∀ x : X.left.fiber,
        e (algebraMap X.left.fiber (AdicCompletion (J.comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber) x) =
          completionUnit (J.map (algebraMap P (henselization P J : Type w))) C
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J).functor.obj X)
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J).henselizationMap X x) := by
  set H := henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) J with hHdef
  set n : Ideal X.left.fiber := J.comap X.hom.map.hom with hndef
  set a : X.left.fiber →+* (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber := H.henselizationMap X with hadef
  have hεa : ((H.henselizationEquiv X).toRingHom.comp
      (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w))) = a :=
    RingHom.ext (H.henselizationEquiv_algebraMap X)
  have hmapε : (n.map (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w))).map
      (H.henselizationEquiv X).toRingHom = n.map a := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map, hεa]
  let e₁ : AdicCompletion n X.left.fiber ≃+*
      AdicCompletion (n.map (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w)))
        (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w) :=
    RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (bijective_adicCompletionMap_henselization X.left.fiber n)
  let e₂ := Rig.adicCompletionCongr (H.henselizationEquiv X)
    (n.map (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w))) (n.map a) hmapε
  let e₃ := adicCompletionEquivOfIdealEq (n.map a)
    ((J.map (algebraMap P (henselization P J : Type w))).comap (H.functor.obj X).hom.map.hom)
    (henselizationDeformation_ideal_comap J X).symm
  refine ⟨e₁.trans (e₂.trans (e₃.val.trans (C.fiberEquiv (H.functor.obj X)).symm)),
    fun x => ?_⟩
  have h₁ : e₁ (algebraMap X.left.fiber (AdicCompletion n X.left.fiber) x) =
      algebraMap (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w)
        (AdicCompletion
          (n.map (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w)))
          (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w))
        (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w) x) :=
    Rig.ofBijective_adicCompletionMap_of _ n _ le_rfl
      (bijective_adicCompletionMap_henselization X.left.fiber n) x
  have h₂ : e₂ (algebraMap (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w)
        (AdicCompletion
          (n.map (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w)))
          (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w))
        (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w) x)) =
      algebraMap (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber
        (AdicCompletion (n.map a) (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber) (a x) :=
    (Rig.adicCompletionCongr_of (H.henselizationEquiv X) _ _ hmapε
      (algebraMap X.left.fiber (henselization X.left.fiber n : Type w) x)).trans
      (congrArg (algebraMap (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber
        (AdicCompletion (n.map a) (H.functor.obj X).left.fiber))
        (H.henselizationEquiv_algebraMap X x))
  show (C.fiberEquiv (H.functor.obj X)).symm (e₃.val (e₂ (e₁ _))) = _
  rw [h₁, h₂, e₃.property]
  rfl

/-! ### The composite decomposition of the completion -/

/-- **The decomposition `R^∧_J ≅ ∏ (R_{𝔪 i})^∧` on elements coming from `R`.** This is the
element-level reading of `Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv`: its `i`-th component
is the canonical map induced by `R → R_{𝔪 i}`. -/
public theorem apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv
    {R : Type w} [CommRing R] {ι : Type uι} [Finite ι] (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum R)
    (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal) (hinj : Function.Injective m) (x : R) (i : ι) :
    adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv m hmax hinj
        (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) R) x) i =
      algebraMap (localRingAt (m i))
        (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i))) (localRingAt (m i)))
        (algebraMap R (localRingAt (m i)) x) := by
  have hle : (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal).map (algebraMap R (localRingAt (m i)))
      ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i)) :=
    (Ideal.map_mono (iInf_le (fun j => (m j).asIdeal) i)).trans_eq
      (IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal (m i).asIdeal (localRingAt (m i)))
  exact adicCompletionMap_apply_algebraMap (algebraMap R (localRingAt (m i)))
    (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i))) hle x

/-- **The completion of `P` along `J = 𝔪 1 ∩ … ∩ 𝔪 n` is the product of the completions of the
henselized local rings `P^h_{𝔪 i}`.** This is
`Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv` followed, factor by factor, by
`Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionHenselizedLocalRingEquiv`; it is the ring isomorphism the
comparison of this file transports along. -/
public noncomputable def adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv
    {ι : Type uι} [Finite ι] (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P)
    (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal) (hinj : Function.Injective m) :
    AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P ≃+*
      (∀ i, AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))) :=
  (adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv m hmax hinj).trans
    (RingEquiv.piCongrRight fun i => adicCompletionHenselizedLocalRingEquiv (m i))

/-- **The composite decomposition, on elements coming from `P`.** The `i`-th component of the
image of `x` is the image of `x` in the completion of the henselization of `P_{𝔪 i}`. -/
public theorem apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv
    {ι : Type uι} [Finite ι] (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P)
    (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal) (hinj : Function.Injective m) (x : P) (i : ι) :
    adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv m hmax hinj
        (algebraMap P (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P) x) i =
      algebraMap (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
        (AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))
        (algebraMap (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
          (algebraMap P (localRingAt (m i)) x)) := by
  show adicCompletionMap (algebraMap (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i))) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) le_rfl
      (adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv m hmax hinj
        (algebraMap P (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P) x) i) = _
  rw [apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv m hmax hinj x i]
  exact adicCompletionMap_apply_algebraMap
    (algebraMap (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i))) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) le_rfl _

/-- **The composite decomposition is `k`-linear**, so it is an isomorphism of `k`-algebras and
`Deformation.Examples.ringDeformationTransport` may be taken along it. Both sides are
`k`-algebras through `P`, and the isomorphism is induced by the `P`-algebra maps
`P → P_{𝔪 i} → P^h_{𝔪 i}`. -/
public theorem algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv
    {ι : Type uι} [Finite ι] (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P)
    (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal) (hinj : Function.Injective m) (a : k) :
    adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv m hmax hinj
        (algebraMap k (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P) a) =
      algebraMap k (∀ i, AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i))
        (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))) a := by
  funext i
  let : IsScalarTower k (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k P (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P),
    apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv m hmax hinj (algebraMap k P a) i,
    Pi.algebraMap_apply,
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
      (AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k P (localRingAt (m i))]

/-! ### The fibre of the completed henselized localized deformation -/

/-- The inverse image of a maximal ideal under a surjection out of a local ring is the maximal
ideal. -/
private theorem comap_eq_maximalIdeal {R S : Type w} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing R]
    (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Surjective f) (I : Ideal S) (hI : I.IsMaximal) :
    I.comap f = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R :=
  IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective f hf (H := hI))

/-- An isomorphism of local rings carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem map_maximalIdeal_ringEquiv {R S : Type w} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsLocalRing S] (e : R ≃+* S) :
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map e.toRingHom = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S := by
  rw [← comap_eq_maximalIdeal e.toRingHom e.surjective (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal S),
    Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective e.toRingHom e.surjective]

/-- **The fibre of the completion of the henselization of the localization of a deformation.**
Localizing a deformation `X` of `P` at `𝔮`, henselizing along the maximal ideal and completing
produces a ring canonically isomorphic to the completion of the local ring of the fibre of `X` at
the inverse image of `𝔮`, and the isomorphism carries the image of `x` to the image of `x`.

Three identifications are composed: the fibre of the localized deformation is *a* localization of
the fibre of `X` at the inverse image of `𝔮`, hence isomorphic to the chosen one; its maximal
ideal is the inverse image of the maximal ideal of `P_𝔮`; and
`Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_henselizedFiber` identifies the completion
at that inverse image with the fibre of the completed henselized deformation. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizedFiber
    (q : PrimeSpectrum P)
    (C : AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
      (henselizedLocalRingAt q) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt q))
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P) :
    ∃ e : AdicCompletion
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q)))
          (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q)) ≃+*
        (C.functor.obj ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt q))).functor.obj
            ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) q.asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj
              X))).left.fiber,
      ∀ x : X.left.fiber,
        e (algebraMap (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q))
            (AdicCompletion
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q)))
              (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q)))
            (algebraMap X.left.fiber
              (localRingAt (PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q)) x)) =
          completionUnit (henselizedMaximalIdealAt q) C
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt q))).functor.obj
                ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) q.asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj X))
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt q))).henselizationMap
                ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) q.asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj X)
              ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) q.asIdeal.primeCompl).localizationMap
                X x)) := by
  classical
  set L := localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) q.asIdeal.primeCompl with hLdef
  set M := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt q) with hMdef
  set H := henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) M with hHdef
  set Y := L.functor.obj X with hYdef
  set p := PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom q with hpdef
  let : Algebra X.left.fiber Y.left.fiber := (L.localizationMap X).toAlgebra
  have : IsLocalization p.asIdeal.primeCompl Y.left.fiber := L.isLocalization X
  have : IsLocalRing Y.left.fiber :=
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing Y.left.fiber p.asIdeal
  let ψ : localRingAt p ≃+* Y.left.fiber :=
    (IsLocalization.algEquiv p.asIdeal.primeCompl (localRingAt p) Y.left.fiber).toRingEquiv
  have hMY : M.comap Y.hom.map.hom = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Y.left.fiber :=
    comap_eq_maximalIdeal Y.hom.map.hom (deformationSpecialFiberMap_surjective Y) M
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal (localRingAt q))
  let eA := Rig.adicCompletionCongr ψ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt p))
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Y.left.fiber) (map_maximalIdeal_ringEquiv ψ)
  let eB := adicCompletionEquivOfIdealEq (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Y.left.fiber)
    (M.comap Y.hom.map.hom) hMY.symm
  obtain ⟨eC, heC⟩ := exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_henselizedFiber M C Y
  refine ⟨eA.trans (eB.val.trans eC), fun x => ?_⟩
  have h₁ : eA (algebraMap (localRingAt p)
        (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt p)) (localRingAt p))
        (algebraMap X.left.fiber (localRingAt p) x)) =
      algebraMap Y.left.fiber
        (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Y.left.fiber) Y.left.fiber)
        (L.localizationMap X x) :=
    (Rig.adicCompletionCongr_of ψ _ _ (map_maximalIdeal_ringEquiv ψ)
      (algebraMap X.left.fiber (localRingAt p) x)).trans
      (congrArg (algebraMap Y.left.fiber
        (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Y.left.fiber) Y.left.fiber))
        ((IsLocalization.algEquiv p.asIdeal.primeCompl (localRingAt p)
          Y.left.fiber).commutes x))
  simp only [RingEquiv.trans_apply]
  rw [h₁, eB.property, heC]

/-! ### The fibre of the completed henselized localized family -/

/-- **The fibre of the completion of a deformation along `J = 𝔪 1 ∩ … ∩ 𝔪 n` is the family of
fibres of the completions of the henselizations of its localizations.** This is the Chinese
remainder decomposition
`Deformation.Examples.bijective_adicCompletion_iInf_to_pi_completedLocalRing` applied to the
fibre of `X` at the family of inverse images of the `𝔪 i` — which are again maximal and distinct,
the reduction of a deformation being surjective — followed factor by factor by
`Deformation.Examples.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizedFiber`. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizationFamilyFiber
    {ι : Type uι} [Finite ι] (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P)
    (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal) (hinj : Function.Injective m)
    (C : ∀ i, AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
      (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)))
    (X : ringDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P) :
    ∃ E : AdicCompletion ((⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal).comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber ≃+*
        (∀ i, ((C i).functor.obj ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i)))).functor.obj
            ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
              (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj X))).left.fiber),
      ∀ (x : X.left.fiber) (i : ι),
        E (algebraMap X.left.fiber
            (AdicCompletion ((⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal).comap X.hom.map.hom) X.left.fiber) x) i =
          completionUnit (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (C i)
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i)))).functor.obj
                ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
                  (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj X))
            ((henselizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i)))).henselizationMap
                ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
                  (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl).functor.obj X)
              ((localizationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
                (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl).localizationMap X x)) := by
  classical
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective X.hom.map.hom := deformationSpecialFiberMap_surjective X
  let q : ι → PrimeSpectrum X.left.fiber := fun i => PrimeSpectrum.comap X.hom.map.hom (m i)
  have hqmax : ∀ i, (q i).asIdeal.IsMaximal := fun i =>
    Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective X.hom.map.hom hsurj
      (K := (m i).asIdeal) (H := hmax i)
  have hqinj : Function.Injective q :=
    (PrimeSpectrum.comap_injective_of_surjective X.hom.map.hom hsurj).comp hinj
  have hJ : (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal).comap X.hom.map.hom = ⨅ j, (q j).asIdeal :=
    Ideal.comap_iInf _ _
  let eJ := adicCompletionEquivOfIdealEq ((⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal).comap X.hom.map.hom)
    (⨅ j, (q j).asIdeal) hJ
  choose E hE using fun i =>
    exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizedFiber (m i) (C i) X
  refine ⟨eJ.val.trans ((adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv q hqmax hqinj).trans
    (RingEquiv.piCongrRight E)), fun x i => ?_⟩
  simp only [RingEquiv.trans_apply, piCongrRight_apply]
  rw [eJ.property, apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionIInfPiEquiv q hqmax hqinj x i, hE i x]

/-! ### The comparison of the two functors -/

/-- An element of `𝔪 i` goes into the maximal ideal of the henselization of `P_{𝔪 i}`. -/
private theorem algebraMap_mem_henselizedMaximalIdealAt {ι : Type uι} (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P)
    (i : ι) {x : P} (hx : x ∈ (m i).asIdeal) :
    algebraMap (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
      (algebraMap P (localRingAt (m i)) x) ∈ henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i) :=
  Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
    ((IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal (m i).asIdeal (localRingAt (m i))).le
      (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hx))

/-- **The structural map from the Artinian base of a product of deformations** is, in each
component, the structural map of that component read through the identification of the bases. -/
public theorem piDeformation_algebraMap_base
    {ι : Type w} [Finite ι] (R : ι → Type w) [∀ i, CommRing (R i)] [∀ i, Algebra k (R i)]
    (A : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, w, w} Λ k)
    (Z : ∀ i, (ringDeformationBasedCategory Λ k (R i)).p.Fiber A)
    (a : ((piDeformation R A Z).left.base : Type w)) (i : ι) :
    algebraMap (((piDeformation R A Z).left.base : Type w))
        (piDeformation R A Z).left.fiber a i =
      algebraMap (((Z i).val.left.base : Type w)) (Z i).val.left.fiber
        ((eqToHom (Z i).property.symm).hom a) :=
  flatAlgebraWithBase_algebraMap A (Z i).val.left (Z i).property a

/-- **A morphism of products of deformations acts componentwise.** -/
public theorem piDeformationFunctor_map_apply
    {ι : Type w} [Finite ι] (R : ι → Type w) [∀ i, CommRing (R i)] [∀ i, Algebra k (R i)]
    {V W : (piBasedCategory fun i => ringDeformationBasedCategory Λ k (R i)).obj}
    (f : V ⟶ W) (y : ((piDeformationFunctor R).obj V).left.fiber) (i : ι) :
    ((piDeformationFunctor R).map f).left.map.hom y i = (f.component i).left.map.hom (y i) :=
  rfl

/-- **Two ring homomorphisms out of an adic completion at a finitely generated ideal agree as
soon as they agree on the image of the base ring.** Both are then the induced map, by
`eq_adicCompletionMap_of_apply_algebraMap`. -/
private theorem adicCompletionMap_ringHom_ext
    {Q B : Type w} [CommRing Q] [CommRing B] (n : Ideal Q) (hn : n.FG) (N : Ideal B)
    (g : Q →+* B) (hg : n.map g ≤ N)
    (α β : AdicCompletion n Q →+* AdicCompletion N B)
    (hα : ∀ z : Q, α (algebraMap Q (AdicCompletion n Q) z) =
      algebraMap B (AdicCompletion N B) (g z))
    (hβ : ∀ z : Q, β (algebraMap Q (AdicCompletion n Q) z) =
      algebraMap B (AdicCompletion N B) (g z)) : α = β := by
  rw [eq_adicCompletionMap_of_apply_algebraMap g n N hg hn α hα,
    eq_adicCompletionMap_of_apply_algebraMap g n N hg hn β hβ]

/-- **The comparison of Stacks 0DZF for the completion leg.** Completing a deformation of `P`
along `J = 𝔪 1 ∩ … ∩ 𝔪 n` and then transporting along a ring isomorphism
`P^∧_J ≅ ∏ (P^h_{𝔪 i})^∧` gives the *same* functor over `𝒞_Λ` as localizing at each `𝔪 i`,
henselizing, completing each henselized local ring, and reading the resulting family as a
deformation of the product ring.

This is the step the source of Stacks 0DZF makes when, having applied **Stacks 0DZ5** to `P`
itself — where the finite type hypothesis genuinely holds — it says "`P^∧ = ∏ P^∧_{𝔪 i}`". The
ring isomorphism and its description on elements coming from `P` are hypotheses, so a caller may
supply the one it already has; `Deformation.Examples.adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv`,
`Deformation.Examples.algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv` and
`Deformation.Examples.apply_algebraMap_adicCompletionPiHenselizedEquiv` are such a triple. -/
@[stacks 0DZF "the identification the source's proof makes when, after applying Stacks 0DZ5 to \
`P` itself with `J = 𝔪 1 ∩ ... ∩ 𝔪 n`, it says `P^ = ∏ P^_{𝔪 i}`: completing a deformation along \
`J` and transporting along a ring isomorphism `P^∧_J ≅ ∏ (P^h_{𝔪 i})^∧` is isomorphic, over \
`𝒞_Λ`, to localizing at each `𝔪 i`, henselizing, completing, and reading the family as a \
deformation of the product ring. Hypotheses: the tag's own on the family -- the `𝔪 i` maximal \
and distinct -- plus `P` of finite type over `k`, and the ring isomorphism together with its \
description on elements of `P`, which are inputs rather than existentials"]
public theorem nonempty_basedIso_adicCompletionFunctor_completionFunctors
    {ι : Type w} [Finite ι] [Algebra.FiniteType k P] [IsNoetherianRing P]
    (m : ι → PrimeSpectrum P) (hmax : ∀ i, (m i).asIdeal.IsMaximal)
    (hinj : Function.Injective m)
    (e : AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P ≃+*
      (∀ i, AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))))
    (he : ∀ a : k, e (algebraMap k (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P) a) =
      algebraMap k (∀ i, AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i))
        (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))) a)
    (hchar : ∀ (x : P) (i : ι),
      e (algebraMap P (AdicCompletion (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal) P) x) i =
        algebraMap (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
          (AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))
          (algebraMap (localRingAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i))
            (algebraMap P (localRingAt (m i)) x))) :
    Nonempty (BasedFunctor.comp
        (adicCompletionFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal)).functor
        (ringDeformationTransport e he) ≅
      BasedFunctor.comp (localizationFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
        (BasedFunctor.comp (henselizationFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
          (BasedFunctor.comp (completionFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
            (piDeformationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) fun i =>
              AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i))
                (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))))) := by
  classical
  have hNoeth : ∀ i : ι, IsNoetherianRing (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)) := fun i =>
    isNoetherianRing_henselizedLocalRingAt (k := k) (m i)
  let D := adicCompletionFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) P (⨅ j, (m j).asIdeal)
  let L : ∀ i : ι, LocalizationFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k) (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl :=
    fun i => localizationFunctor (m i).asIdeal.primeCompl
  let H : ∀ i : ι, HenselizationFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
      (P := localRingAt (m i)) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i))) :=
    fun i => henselizationFunctor (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (localRingAt (m i)))
  let C : ∀ i : ι, AdicCompletionFunctorData (Λ := Λ) (k := k)
      (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) :=
    fun i => adicCompletionFunctor (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)) (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i))
  have hC : ∀ i, (C i).IsBaseCompatible := fun i =>
    isBaseCompatible_adicCompletionFunctor _ _
  choose E5 hE5 using fun X =>
    exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_completedLocalizationFamilyFiber m hmax hinj C X
  let F := BasedFunctor.comp D.functor (ringDeformationTransport e he)
  let G := BasedFunctor.comp (localizationFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
    (BasedFunctor.comp (henselizationFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
      (BasedFunctor.comp (completionFunctors (Λ := Λ) (k := k) m)
        (piDeformationFunctor (Λ := Λ) (k := k) fun i =>
          AdicCompletion (henselizedMaximalIdealAt (m i)) (henselizedLocalRingAt (m i)))))
  refine ⟨basedIsoOfFiberEquiv F G (fun X => (D.fiberEquiv X).trans (E5 X)) ?_ ?_ ?_⟩
  · -- linearity over the Artinian base
    intro X a
    set a' := (eqToHom (basedFunctor_base_eq F G X)).hom a with ha'
    set a₀ := (eqToHom (D.functor.w_obj X)).hom a with ha₀
    have h6 : (D.fiberEquiv X)
